course: dictionary
lesson: 3688
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the sentence around the word, because the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The cat flap let the cat in and out all night.» Here flap is a small door, not a movement.
explain: Flap can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it means to move quickly up and down or from side to side: «An African elephant flaps its huge ears» to cool down. As a noun it means a flat piece that covers an opening, like the flap of an envelope.
explain: Ask yourself: is something moving, or is there a flat piece covering a gap? Then put your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one. Informally, «in a flap» means worried and in a fuss.
fact: Flap can mean to move up and down or side to side quickly, like a bird's wings or a flag in the wind.
fact: A flap is a flat piece of paper, cloth or other material fixed along one side that covers an opening.
fact: «Don't get in a flap» means don't get worried or in a fuss.
fact: «A sugar glider has a skin flap between its front and back legs» and uses it to glide from tree to tree.
fact: A good check for two meanings is to read the words around the word and ask which meaning fits best.
exercise: «The stoats were in a flap, running all ways.» What does in a flap mean here? | Asleep in the warm | *Worried and in a fuss | Flying high above the trees
exercise: «A sugar glider has a skin flap between its front and back legs.» What is the flap? | A pocket for food | *A flat piece of skin that helps it glide | A kind of tree
exercise: «The alligator snapping turtle lures fish with a pink worm-shaped flap on its tongue.» What is the flap? | A shell on its back | A type of weed | A fish hook | *A flap of skin shaped like a worm
test: What does flap mean in «flap its wings»? | To close a door quietly | *To move up and down quickly | Worried and in a fuss | A piece of cloth on a tent
test: What is a cat flap? | *A small door that lets a cat in and out | A cage for a bird | A tall gate in a garden | A bed for a cat
exam: Ella reads «lift the flap» in a book. What is she lifting? | A tent pole | *A flat paper cover over a picture | A heavy box | A bird's wing
